$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }r\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-1})+(\goldD{-8})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-\dfrac{9}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $h\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{9}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
h\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{9}{2}}\right)&=\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{9}{2}}+1\right)\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{9}{2}}+8\right)
\\\\
&=\left(-\dfrac72\right)\left(\dfrac72\right)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{49}{4}
\end{align}$
